<figure class="cache-figure" data-cache-rollout>
 <p class="figure-title">A cold namespace spends the source’s spare capacity</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Traffic on new namespace <input data-share type="range" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="20" /><output data-share-label></output></label><label>New namespace hit rate <input data-hit type="range" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="0" /><output data-hit-label></output></label></div>
 <p class="figure-note">1,000 requests/s total · old namespace stays at 95% hits · source budget 200 loads/s</p>
 <div class="ops-rollout-paths"><div><b>Old namespace</b><strong data-old-requests></strong><span>↓ 5% miss</span><strong data-old-loads></strong></div><div><b>New namespace</b><strong data-new-requests></strong><span data-new-miss></span><strong data-new-loads></strong></div></div>
 <p class="figure-note">Combined source demand · scale 0–1,000 loads/s · marker at 200</p>
 <div class="ops-source-budget"><i class="ops-old" data-old-bar></i><i class="ops-new" data-new-bar></i><b></b></div>
 <p data-total class="cluster-command"></p><p data-explanation class="explanation" aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>This steady-rate model assumes one source load per miss, no coalescing, and no extra refresh traffic. The new hit rate is an input representing a measured cohort, not a promise that waiting will warm every workload. The budget is invented. Old and new colours keep their identity as traffic and source demand change.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{rolloutLoad}from'../../lib/caching/operations.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cache-rollout]').forEach(root=>{const share=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-share]')!,hit=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-hit]')!;const fmt=(n:number)=>Number(n.toFixed(1)).toString();const render=()=>{const s=rolloutLoad(Number(share.value),Number(hit.value));for(const[k,v]of Object.entries({'share-label':`${share.value}%`,'hit-label':`${hit.value}%`,'old-requests':`${fmt(s.oldRequests)} requests/s`,'new-requests':`${fmt(s.newRequests)} requests/s`,'old-loads':`${fmt(s.oldLoads)} source loads/s`,'new-loads':`${fmt(s.newLoads)} source loads/s`,'new-miss':`↓ ${100-Number(hit.value)}% miss`,'total':`${fmt(s.total)} source loads/s · ${s.excess?`${fmt(s.excess)} above budget`:`${fmt(s.budget-s.total)} below budget`}`}))root.querySelector(`[data-${k}]`)!.textContent=v;root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-old-bar]')!.style.width=`${s.oldLoads/10}%`;root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-new-bar]')!.style.width=`${s.newLoads/10}%`;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s.excess?'This rollout exceeds the assumed source budget. Reduce the traffic step or establish enough reuse before increasing it. Retries would add work which this model does not include.':'Demand fits this assumed budget. Confirm real source latency, errors, concurrency and cache freshness before the next step; spare capacity in one model is not a deployment approval.';};share.oninput=render;hit.oninput=render;render();});
</script>
